# Line endings are pinned here instead of being left to each contributor's
# core.autocrlf. A CRLF checkout of a shipped hook is not cosmetic: bash reads
# `then\r` as a command, so the hook dies mid-verdict and every tool call it
# gates is denied with a syntax error (probe-verified: exit 2).
*.sh                        text eol=lf
plugin/bin/oso-state        text eol=lf
plugin/git-hooks/pre-commit text eol=lf

# The Windows entrypoints pin what already ships: both files are LF in this tree
# today, so LF is the form that has actually been exercised. CRLF would be the
# conventional Windows choice, but switching would ship a form nothing here has
# run — and bootstrap/verify.sh check 11 scans both for CR bytes either way.
*.ps1                       text eol=lf
*.bat                       text eol=lf
